# A free-roam streetcar behaves like the race's: standing on the outbound J track in Dolores Park, on the
# straight north of the street that crosses the park, you wait for the inbound car (1000000) to turn back at
# 18th Street. Coming south at its cruise, it rings its bell once, 25 m off, then hits you at 11 m/s ("hit by
# a streetcar") and throws you off the track; it runs on. (The F no longer runs. The spot is one where the
# lawn is level with the track: in most places the car's route height sits above the lawn and it misses you.)
park sf
cmd 0 traffic clear
cmd 0 streetcars on
cmd 1 teleport -402.90 -164.85 22.9 123
run 8200
expect event honk{car=1000000,robo=false,tram=true} within 7442..7442
expect event honk count == 1
expect event carHit{car=1000000,robo=false,speed=11,reason=hit by a streetcar} within 7709..7709
expect event bail{reason=hit by a streetcar} within 7709..7709
expect event carHit count == 1
expect event recover within 7859..7859
